{
  "archival_report": "The project processed a request for a scale drawing illustration of a rectangular park with a 10:4 side ratio, based on an educational problem statement involving scale conversion (1 cm = 90 m). Initial validation classified the request as a visual illustration task ('STANDARD_DIAGRAM' route) requiring both strict mathematical precision (exact 10:4 aspect ratio, dimension arrows, scale legend) and artistic rendering (top-down park assets). During scaffolding generation in Matplotlib, the first code iteration was flagged during visual inspection for edge clipping: automatic whitespace cropping truncated the '4 cm' text label on the left margin and the 'Scale: 1 cm = 90 m' legend box in the bottom right corner. This was remediated in Attempt 2 by expanding the coordinate spatial limits with invisible anchor points (ax.scatter) and shifting labels inward, passing all reviewer checks. During the subsequent artistic finishing pass, the AI image generator failed its initial rendering attempt due to two primary issues: leaving a flat, unrendered green circle primitive in the bottom-left corner that spilled over the park boundary, and hallucinating an unrequested duplicate '4 cm' dimension line on the right side of the rectangle. A targeted prompt retry was executed, instructing the model to fully render all corner primitives, strictly enforce the rectangular bounding box, and omit any dimension lines on the right side. The final regenerated image successfully resolved these defects, delivering an aesthetically rich, mathematically accurate diagram that met all QA criteria.",
  "system_improvement_suggestions": [
    "Incorporate automatic padding rules or invisible anchor points by default in the Matplotlib code generator templates to prevent label and text box clipping during tight bounding box exports.",
    "Enhance artist prompt templates for standard scaffolding transformations to explicitly instruct generative models to render or remove all raw geometric primitives, preventing unrendered blockouts from appearing in final image passes.",
    "Add explicit negative prompts regarding symmetric duplication of measurement annotations to prevent generative models from hallucinating mirrored dimension lines."
  ]
}
